  "context_pill": "Capital Gains: HUF Partition & Improvement Cost",
  "example_summary": "Land purchased by HUF in P.Y. 2002-03 for 1,20,000 was allotted to Mr. A in P.Y. 2006-07 partition (valued at 1,50,000). Mr. A spent 2,35,000 on fencing in P.Y. 2007-08 and sold it in June 2025 for 15,00,000 with 20,000 transfer expense.",
  "source_provision": "| Statutory Area | Legal Provision | Core Rule |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Cost Determination | Section 49(1) | COA = Cost to the previous owner |\n| Improvement Cost | Section 55(2) | Actual expenditure for capital improvement |\n| Transfer Expenses | Section 48 | Deductible from Full Value of Consideration |\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Section 49(1) Scope: \nWhen a capital asset is acquired by the assessee by way of partition of HUF, the cost of acquisition is deemed to be the cost to the previous owner (the HUF), as adjusted by any cost of improvement incurred by the previous owner or the assessee.\n\n> [!WARNING] Expenditure Traps:\n- Expenses must be incurred exclusively for the transfer of the asset.\n- Cost of improvement must be capital in nature; revenue expenditure is ineligible for deduction under Section 48.\n\n### Computation Framework:\n1. Full Value of Consideration (-) Transfer Expenses = Net Consideration\n2. Net Consideration (-) Cost of Acquisition (u/s 49(1)) (-) Cost of Improvement = Capital Gain",
